<section>
<title>Detailed Description</title>

<para>Input cleaning and sanitization utilities.</para>

<para>Provides safe access to command-line arguments, GET, and POST variables, plus sanitizers for PIDs, ports, service names, file paths, and HTML output.</para>

<para>Usage: <literallayout><computeroutput>$action&#32;=&#32;<link linkend="_class_util_input_1a36df364a60f90190e825d2879d65c9f3">UtilInput::cleanArgv</link>(1);
$page&#32;&#32;&#32;=&#32;<link linkend="_class_util_input_1a9b6dbda34fb81d34ec2b9bd461c03e08">UtilInput::cleanGetVar</link>(<emphasis role="charliteral">&apos;p&apos;</emphasis>);
$pid&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;=&#32;<link linkend="_class_util_input_1a9531f06224fb7905b4e7541350711e00">UtilInput::sanitizePID</link>($rawPid);
</computeroutput></literallayout> </para>
<para>
Definition at line <link linkend="_class_8util_8input_8php_source_1l00024">24</link> of file <link linkend="_class_8util_8input_8php_source">class.util.input.php</link>.</para>
</section>
